    },
    {
      "ordinal": 60,
      "label": "original_book_honbun_15_01",
      "hash64": "F6CB892D7DBCB272",
      "text": "While separated from the research\\nteam in the crater’s depths, I found\\na strange...entity. Whether it was a\\nPokémon, or even alive at all, I\\nknow not. It bore a shell with\\nlayers of overlapping hexagons, and\\ngleamed brighter still than gemstone.\\nViewed as a whole, it resembled a\\nmysterious, brilliant disk.",
      "flags": 0,
      "text_status": "DECODED",
      "label_encoding_status": "UTF8",
      "label_raw_hex": null,
      "tokens": []
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 61,
      "label": "original_book_title_16_01",
      "hash64": "4AC9E3F15BCBFE13",
      "text": "A Disk Pokémon?",
      "flags": 4,
      "text_status": "DECODED",
      "label_encoding_status": "UTF8",
      "label_raw_hex": null,
      "tokens": []
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 62,
      "label": "original_book_honbun_16_01",
      "hash64": "FAD6494450B28B05",
      "text": "I have tentatively named this\\ncreature Terapagos. I suspect that\\nits very body is made up of the key\\nmaterial that causes Pokémon to\\nshine brightly and crystallize.",
      "flags": 4,
      "text_status": "DECODED",
